{
  "schema": "cross-survival-layer-capacity-v1",
  "definition": "Conditional on the proposed drop leaving no CROSS landing, before any clear every new cell in its column is above the previous top. A layer with a buried empty cell cannot be the first to clear. For each remaining candidate layer and piece, translate every distinct one-level shape footprint into that layer’s current holes. The largest fitting footprint upper-bounds the contribution of any future placement of that piece before a clear. Allow reuse of holes and ignore supporting geometry and the other slice levels to stay optimistic. For a possible set of pieces before CROSS, if the upper sum misses every layer, no sequence of legal placements can restore CROSS by its arrival. The score is the exact public probability mass of subsets for which this impossibility is proved. A lower bound below one does not establish that a clear is achievable.",
  "public_information": "Observed piece counts after the drop and the original visible preview. Within the bag containing the next CROSS, each rank has equal probability. Each k-piece preceding subset of the unknown n non-CROSS shapes has mass 1/((n+1)*C(n,k)). If the current bag already spent CROSS, all remaining current-bag pieces precede a new uniform bag. No hidden RNG enters the score.",
  "planned_archive": {
    "registered_utc": "2026-11-26T16:45:51+00:00",
    "study": "public-cross-clear-deadline-v1",
    "inputs": {
