    },
    "cohort": "All 67 previously identified positive-to-zero CROSS transitions from 64 preselected training streams, including all three recorded clear recoveries; additionally the eight previously published cold terminal boards separately. No new outcome selection, new policy decisions or sealed data.",
    "question": "Immediately after the decisive drop, can any clear happen before the next CROSS? Give a rigorous public lower bound on the probability of unavoidable death by that arrival, conditional on the visible piece and counts, uniformly averaging compatible bag orderings. Use the recorded future only to test the bound against observed outcomes.",
    "physics": "Before the first clear all newly occupied cells in a column must land strictly above its highest occupied cell. Any layer with a buried hole is excluded. For an accessible layer, bound each non-CROSS piece contribution by the largest single-level footprint that can fit its existing holes, ignoring gravity/other levels and reusing holes across different hypothetical moves. A clear requires total possible contribution at least the number of missing cells in some layer. Test nested screen using missing cells and catalog maximum footprint only as control.",
    "bag": "At post-action time use only placed counts and the one originally visible next piece. Enumerate subsets that can precede the next CROSS under uniform bags. Aggregate order-independent subset capacities with exact combinatorial weights. Record separately universal certificates and conditional lower bounds.",
    "checks": "Reproduce source hashes, gravity, each clear, every transition and final board hash. For each actual recovered interval require the realized intervening pieces can cover some layer, public forced probability <1. Compare cheap versus footprint bound and actual matched subset. No policy promotion from archive outcomes."
